         The encluded script files are used to log on to Telnet's PC
         Pursuit.  Pcpx12 and Pcpx24 are for the Net, and nbbs12 and
         nbbs24 are for the new BBS.
              Install these scripts in your dialing directory with the
         number for your local net at 1200 or 2400 baud.  You can call
         in at any parity, the script sets 8n1.


              The ice script I assign to one of the "F" keys,
         ie;@ice^M.  Then any time you need to recall ICEX its handy.
         Also do not use auto logon, assign name and password to keys.
         Seems to work very well for me.

         ENJOY,
               Randy Risher
